. **No mass product design is timeless.**  \n   If a design is a mass product (\\(MP\\)), it is not timeless (\\(\\neg T\\)):  \n   \\(MP \\rightarrow \\neg T\\).\n\n3. **Either Zaha Hadid's design style or Kelly Wearstler's design style.**  \n   Every design is in either ZH's style or KW's style:  \n   For any design \\(d\\), \\(S_Z(d) \\lor S_K(d)\\).\n\n4. **All of Kelly Wearstler's design styles are evocative.**  \n   If a design is in KW's style, it is evocative (\\(E\\)).\n\n5. **All of Kelly Wearstler's design styles are dreamy.**  \n   If a design is in KW's style, it is dreamy (\\(D\\)).\n\n6. **If a design by Max is timeless, then it is a mass product design and evocative.**  \n   For any Max design \\(m\\), \\(T(m) \\rightarrow (MP(m) \\land E(m))\\).\n\n---\n\n### **Analysis:**\nConsider a design \\(m\\) by Max. We need to determine if \\(MP(m)\\) is necessarily true, false, or uncertain.\n\n",
