s a member of both. So combining both sentences, the information holds. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer should be A) True.\n</think>\n\nA) True\n\n**Explanation:**  \nThe context explicitly states that Heinrich Schmidt was a Nazi German politician and a member of both the Prussian State Parliament and the Nazi Reichstag. The statement in question asks whether \"some\" Nazi German politician held both roles. Since Heinrich Schmidt is provided as an example of such a person, the existence of even one individual satisfies the existential claim (\"some\"). Thus, the statement is **True**. The typo in the name (\"Heeinrich\") does not negate the factual information provided about his roles.",
